    "title": "Growing Research Reveals Potential Link Between Eye Health & Dementia Risk - NewsBreak",
    "text": "21 hours ago Your eyes may reveal more about your brain than you think. Early research from Rutgers University suggests that tiny abnormalities in the blood vessels of your eyes could signal early changes in the brain linked to dementia, potentially years before symptoms appear. While this research is still ongoing, scientists are hopeful that one day, eye imaging could help identify people at risk for cognitive decline. Here's what you need to know. Read full article",
